<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48938" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĕcēnārĭus</span></b>  (
		TERCENARIVS, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 387, 8</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">417, 5</span></i>), a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. num.</i> [treceni]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to three
				hundred</i>: vites, i. e. <i>that yield three
				hundred</i> amphorae <i>of wine to the juger</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 2, 7</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A soldier whose pay is three hundred</i> sestertia
			(cf. ducenarius), <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 365, 6</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">387, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">417, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
